        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Earth Glide"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "The guecubu can Burrow through any earthen matter, including rock. When it does so, the guecubu moves at its full burrow Speed, leaving no tunnels or signs of its passing."
            },
            "id": "2806a284-e16b-4b32-8ece-7e97dfe020f7",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-03-17T12:41:27.494111"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Shove into Stone"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "(arcane, earth, transmutation)\n\nWhen the guecubu successfully Shoves a creature into a stone barrier, the target must succeed at a DC 26 Reflex save or become merged with the barrier, with the effects of meld into stone until the target Escapes (DC 26)."
            },
            "id": "3064dcc7-09cf-4d8f-bd72-708f8c1e28bf",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-03-17T12:41:27.494111"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Wrathful Misfortune"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "(arcane, curse, enchantment)\n\nA creature damaged by a guecubu must succeed at a DC 26 Will save or become cursed with consummate bad luck. The creature becomes clumsy 2. Each time that creature rolls initiative, on their next roll they must roll twice and use the worse result; this is a misfortune effect."
            },
            "id": "8ede7adf-ad54-4e81-8756-3c5314501a20",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-03-17T12:41:27.494111"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
